        "review": [
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DOREENBUCH"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are GREAT!!! I love them w/ the Fiesta Ranch Dip, too!!! Also, to prevent flour tortilla's from tearing, either let them set to room temp, or microwave them -- when they are warm, they will roll up easily."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am shocked at the reviews some people gave. I have made these things for the last year, because after the first time, people FREAKED out, I have not had ANYONE not like them. Not sure what people are talking about them being too salty, someone's not doing something right, these things are DIVINE! I use about 20 small \"taco size\" tortillas thought and use orange bell pepper, found the taste of orange is the best. \r\nThis has been the BEST recipe on this site!",
            "datePublished": "2003-12-22T09:58:31.380Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MTMLMM_96"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely fantastic!! I made them for a party of fifty with ages ranging from 8-55. I was scared that nobody would eat them...but they were ooed and awed about all night. I made them with half the amount of ranch mix. I also used three different kinds of tortillas...MISSION spinach, sun dried tomatoes and zesty. It was such a beautiful way to display these little beauties! I am also happy to say that I ran out before the party was over (I doubled the recipe). Enjoy!!",
            "datePublished": "2002-11-08T13:06:56.983Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DJACKS73"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my favorite quick appetizer to make. I had problems at first trying to keep them from unrolling after I sliced them. Then, I figured out that if you spread cream cheese all the way to the end of the tortilla, leaving the last quarter inch or so with only cream cheese spread and no veggies, the cream cheese acts like a glue and the tortilla will stick together. Aha!",
            "datePublished": "2008-12-13T10:37:54.570Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RENAEF"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are fabulous! Everytime I make them my family goes crazy. Instead of using the sliced black olives I use a can of the diced olives - that way you still get the flavor but not the awkwardness of the sliced olives sliding out while biting into them - and it is easier to spread onto the tortillas! I also use 34 of the ranch dip packet. DELICIOUS!",
            "datePublished": "2003-11-18T21:21:06.077Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe, I have used this several times. If you think it sounds good but don't want the hassle buy spreadable graden vegtable cream cheese instead. Excellent recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2002-06-30T13:43:42.700Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DREGINEK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I halved the recipe because of all the \"too salty\" complaints and before I ruined an entire batch, I thought I'd try half first. It IS a tad on the salty side but they were delicious (which means, when I make the \"full\" version, I will just use half a pkg of dry ranch dressing). As another reviewer stated, the veggie combinations are endless...although I followed the recipe to the letter the first time. Thanks to my handy-dandy chopper, I was able to mince all my veggies, which made it even better. Thanks Linda!!",
            "datePublished": "2003-01-02T17:30:31.903Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Foodie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were so good. You could really put anything in them. I decreased the amount of ranch dressing. I thought it was getting too salty. I will make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2007-06-25T21:35:34.053Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Navy_Mommy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are very good and super easy to make. I will take them to potlucks all the time. I didn't add the celery to mine because I didn't have any, but really you can add just about any colorful vegetable that you like. I have made with roasted peppers before and that is really good too.",
            "datePublished": "2003-06-04T08:41:07.657Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this recipe several times for various occasions and it has always been a hit. In earlier reviews it was suggested that you use half the amount of ranch dressing mix to cut the salt content. That's all you have to change from the original to have success. To make the process easier I mix all ingredients together then spread onto the tortillas. It saves a lot of time and makes less of a mess but it tastes the same. I think people that didn't like it should try again using less of the dressing mix. I'm sure it'll work for you then.",
            "datePublished": "2006-08-09T14:45:53.750Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "StephG"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very very good. I made it for husband's work pot luck. I added extra block of cream cheese (based on what was said regarding saltiness) to cut salt and to have extras. I nuked the tortillas for 10 secs. first to help with pliability, because you can't be shy about rolling these babies up tight!",
            "datePublished": "2004-05-18T15:21:00.937Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JimmyHelfer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious. The ranch mix and green onions in the cream cheese added a great bit of zing. I added some ham cold cuts to some of them. Next time I will some jalapenos.",
            "datePublished": "2026-02-27T20:35:25.853Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AmLost2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used about 2/3 pkg of ranch seasoning and it turned out great.",
            "datePublished": "2026-02-12T18:20:29.708Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "knittygirl52"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this twice over the holidays. The first time I got them all rolled up and realized I forgot the shredded cheddar! Oh well. We ate them anyway, and enjoyed them as was. The second time I remembered the cheddar. We still ate and enjoyed them. Guess what? I like them both ways, but I seriously preferred them without. (Can’t tell you what others thought. I just know they scarfed them down.)",
            "datePublished": "2026-01-12T02:23:24.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Andrea Fraser Hanson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are pretty good as is, however next time I will add deli meat and cheese. I did add jalapenos to half, and I liked those better, but I'm not big on bell peppers. I will make again, as they're easy, attractive, and flavorful. Variations should be limitless! Pimentos would be good too!",
            "datePublished": "2026-01-09T19:41:57.483Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
